  "aciklama": "Van Norman Dam nearly failed in the San Fernando earthquake. The cause: liquefaction of hydraulic fill causing a landslide that took part of the crest.\n\nFailure chain: Hydraulic fill Dam → Earthquake → Fill liquefies → Crest slides into reservoir → Emergency drawdown\n\nAnother reconstruction: The Disaster That Ended the Age of the Airship — https://youtu.be/PGOKZhPYo7c\n\nFootage & sources:\n• Archival film: \"Lower Van Norman Dam Damage 1971.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lower_Van_Norman_Dam_Damage_1971.jpg\n• Archival film: \"Earthquake Damaged Dam (22190042935).jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Earthquake_Damaged_Dam_(22190042935).jpg\n• Archival film: \"USGS - 1971 San Fernando earthquake - Damage at Lower Van Norman Dam.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:USGS_-_1971_San_Fernando_earthquake_-_Damage_at_Lower_Van_Norman_Dam.jpg\n• Archival film: \"LAD 4 Binder2 008 - USACE-p15141coll5-18850.jpeg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LAD_4_Binder2_008_-_USACE-p15141coll5-18850.jpeg\n• Archival film: \"Van Norman Dam 1971 eq 0.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Van_Norman_Dam_1971_eq_0.jpg\n\nTechnical references:\n• Wikipedia — Lower Van Norman Dam — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lower_Van_Norman_Dam\n• USGS — report (cited by Wikipedia) — https://pubs.usgs.gov/circ/1974/0691a/report.pdf\n\nNarration uses a synthetic voice. Footage is real archival film or licensed stock; anything reconstructed is labelled on screen.\n\n#Shorts #VanNormanDam #SanFernandoEarthquake #DamFailure #Liquefaction #EngineeringDisaster #CivilEngineering #EarthquakeEngineering #Infrastructure #FailureAnalysis",
